  "name": "Semeiskie song (Transbaikal Old Believer polyphony)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Semeiskie are Old Believers deported to Transbaikalia in the second half of the 18th century from the western frontier lands where they had taken refuge; they settled in villages such as Tarbagatay in present-day Buryatia and kept their dress, rites and songs. Their drawn-out lyrical and ritual songs are sung in dense multi-voiced polyphony, and UNESCO proclaimed the cultural space and oral culture of the Semeiskie a Masterpiece of the Oral and Intangible Heritage of Humanity.",
  "recipe": "classic modern semeiskie song, drone Modal, vocal branch. many notes per syllable, choral, single lead single track no stacking. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
